  $bow$# Grade 6 MAPEH — Budget of Work

MAPEH is graded as two components — Music & Arts, and Physical Education & Health — each with its own quarterly grade that is then averaged. Both sequences below follow the official Grade 6 curriculum guide tables verbatim. Grade Level Standard for PE & Health: "The learners evaluate complex health practices, movements, and fitness skills in promoting personal, family, community, and societal wellness for active and healthy living."

## Term 1: Music & Arts — Development in Music and Arts in the Revolutionary Period (1801-1898); PE & Health — Holistic Wellness & Target/Invasion Games
- **Music:** Timbre (instrumental ensembles, vocal styles/techniques) and dynamics (dynamic markings) as heard in sacred and secular vocal/instrumental music of the period; active listening, describing, and performing (singing, moving, playing).
- **Arts (Theater/Dance):** Relevant theater forms and their subjects/themes/symbolisms from the period, with focus on character and conflict; dance forms and their role in different time periods.
- **Health (Personal Health, real Grade 6 content):** Content Standard — holistic wellness, changes in health dimensions during adolescence. Explaining the interdependence of the dimensions of holistic wellness (physical, mental/intellectual, emotional, social/relational, spiritual, occupational, cultural/creative, financial, environmental); evaluating how changes in these dimensions affect adolescents' well-being; engaging in physical and other activities to improve holistic wellness.
- **PE (Target and/or Invasion Games, real Grade 6 content):** Executing modified physical activities (target/invasion games such as modified sports) applying movement concepts, locomotor/manipulative skills, and fitness concepts (agility, balance, coordination, speed) for active living. Performance Standard: participating in modified target/invasion games and other physical activities in promoting personal wellness.

**Special Science enrichment:** hindi inilalapat sa asignaturang MAPEH.

## Term 2: Music & Arts — Development of Philippine Music and Arts in the American Colonial Period (1898-1935); PE & Health — Sexual and Reproductive Health & Striking/Fielding or Net/Wall Games
- **Music:** Rhythm (meter, time signatures, rhythmic dance patterns) and tempo (musical symbols/terms for speed), drawn from Philippine classical, semi-classical, and popular music of the period.
- **Arts (Theater/Dance):** Symbolic theater and seditious plays, focusing on dramatic structure; dance forms of the period and their role.
- **Health (Sexual and Reproductive Health, real Grade 6 content):** Content Standard — early pregnancy prevention, family dynamics on teenage concerns. Discussing the benefits of developing healthy and positive sexuality and preventing early pregnancy (understanding healthy sexuality, identifying sexual risk behaviors, practicing assertive/refusal skills toward abstinence, safeguarding sexual and reproductive health); evaluating the family's role in helping adolescents deal with sexual and reproductive health concerns, particularly teenage-pregnancy prevention.
- **PE (Striking/Fielding and/or Net/Wall Games, real Grade 6 content):** Executing modified physical activities (striking/fielding or net/wall games such as modified sports) applying the concepts and skills for active living. Performance Standard: participating in modified striking/fielding and/or net/wall games in promoting family wellness.

**Special Science enrichment:** hindi inilalapat sa asignaturang MAPEH.

## Term 3: Music & Arts — Development of Music and Arts during the Commonwealth Period and Japanese Occupation (1935-1946); PE & Health — Disease Prevention and Control & Rhythmic Activities and Dances
- **Music:** Melody (tonality/mode) and harmony (basic accompaniment), drawn from folk music relevant to the period and region; listening, creating, performing, evaluating.
- **Arts (Theater/Dance):** Symbolic theater and seditious plays with focus on staging and spectacle; dance forms of the period.
- **Health (Disease Prevention and Control, real Grade 6 content):** Content Standard — prevention and control of common communicable diseases. Explaining the nature (characteristics, emergence/resurgence, disease agents, transmission) of common communicable diseases affecting learners (chicken pox, common cold, conjunctivitis, hepatitis, influenza, measles, meningitis, poliomyelitis, mumps, pertussis, pneumonia, rubella, scabies, tuberculosis, malaria, bronchitis, COVID-related infections, typhoid fever, leptospirosis, vector-borne diseases such as dengue/zika/chikungunya); analyzing prevention and control (stages of infection, breaking the chain of infection, importance of vaccination/immunization); evaluating physical activity's benefits as an immune-boosting measure.
- **PE (Rhythmic Activities and Dances, real Grade 6 Q3 content):** Dance Exercise, exercises with light apparatus, dance movements (local street dance and festival), and/or traditional dances with implements (sticks, scarf, bamboo castanets), leading actively to sustain movement competence. Performance Standard: participating in rhythmic activities, dances, and other physical activities in promoting community wellness.

**Special Science enrichment:** hindi inilalapat sa asignaturang MAPEH.

## Term 4: Music & Arts — "My Filipino Identity" (Contemporary Period); PE & Health — Environmental Health & Rhythmic Activities and Dances
- **Music:** Texture (monophony, homophony, polyphony, heterophony) and form (free-form, strophic, binary, ternary), in the context of the Philippine contemporary period; composing, performing, reflecting.
- **Arts (Theater/Dance):** Performance practices in Philippine history that present and celebrate Filipino identities, applying elements of drama (character, plot, setting); dance forms focused on communicative function.
- **Health (Environmental Health, real Grade 6 content):** Content Standard — environmental issues/concerns, sanitation. Discussing environmental concerns using the concept of One Health (air quality, chemical safety, climate change, emergency preparedness, food safety, healthy housing, infectious disease and vector control, occupational safety and health, solid waste management, water supply and sanitation) and their harmful effects on human and animal health; evaluating strategies for managing and promoting environmental health sanitation through community participation (environmental health monitoring, hygiene promotion, solid waste management [8Rs], wastewater management, pest/vector control); advocating for environmental health protection through physical activity (outdoor recreation, active transportation, green exercise).
- **PE (Rhythmic Activities and Dances, real Grade 6 Q4 content):** Dance Exercise, dance movements (regional street dance and festival), and/or traditional dances (national dances), leading actively to sustain movement competence. Performance Standard: participating in environmental promotion, rhythmic activities, and dances in promoting societal wellness.
- **Year-end project:** Produce a contemporary creative work (Music & Arts) depicting historical/cultural/national identity, using relevant concepts and practices from across the year, alongside a PE/Health showcase — together forming the MAPEH culmination for Key Stage 2.

**Special Science enrichment:** hindi inilalapat sa asignaturang MAPEH.$bow$,
